{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/93327-is-it-really-wrong-to-like-the-week-of-nightmares","id":93327,"title":"Is it really wrong to like the Week of Nightmares?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-03-18T02:19:13-07:00","id":93327,"title":"Is it really wrong to like the Week of Nightmares?","content":"I am Eldagusto, and I enjoyed the Week of Nightmares. I thought it was neat, I enjoyed the insanely convoluted backstory to it (it wasn't a bug it was a feature, the ultimate Easter Egg hunt), and how most beings only knew a small fraction of the story and assumed it was responsible for everything else. And I liked the Crossovery goodness, and that an Antediluvian Died. At the moment I can't think of anything that offended me from its handling.<br /> <br /> Though wait I do have one question some have said it was the relics of Fatman and Littleboy that were used on Enoch's Ghost, but that seems very odd since the Smiling Lord harvested his Relic nukes from the desert testing site in America, so they should have been the test nukes like the I have become Shiva nuke. Because if anything wouldn't the Fatman and Little Boy Nukes more likely be in the Hands of Yu Huang or the Japanese Rebels?<br /> <br /> But yeah I completely Embrace the Week of Nightmares Reckoning Eye of the Wyrm event! I can't be the only one right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-18T04:00:04-07:00","id":93361,"title":"","content":"No it's not strange at all. I too like the Week of Nightmares, the Sixth Great Maelstrom and the Avatar Storm.<br /> <br /> As for the nukes, one I know was the goal in one of the chronicles in the Dark Kingdom of Jade Adventure book and it's implied that's how it ended up in the Smiling Lord's hands. The other one I'm not sure about but I think Yu Huuang gave it to the Smiling Lord as part of their plans for the invasion of the Dark Kingdom of Iron.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-18T07:56:41-07:00","id":93493,"title":"","content":"Ohhh, I need to read the Adventures book, I have it in Solid form but its not accessible to me at the moment. Thanks that clarifies things.<br /> <br /> I get the impression a lot that people shouldn't like the Week of Nightmares if they were good upstanding blokes. I mean its not like the return of Samuel Height or anything, I thought it was cool and still do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-18T09:42:01-07:00","id":93538,"title":"","content":"For me the essential problem comes back to the Vampires not getting any face time with their own metaplot. The Antediluvians are supposed to be the terrifying apocalyptic villains of the setting, and one got taken out (with minimal effort) by the Kue-Jin and the Technocracy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-18T10:02:41-07:00","id":93548,"title":"","content":"No, there's nothing wrong with liking it. I think most of the disdain toward it is directed at the idea of forced metaplot changes to the setting and not at the actual event itself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/260-chase-variant","name":"Chase Variant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar260_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"150"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-18T10:07:46-07:00","id":93553,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caitiff Primogen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/93327-is-it-really-wrong-to-like-the-week-of-nightmares?p=93538#post93538\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For me the essential problem comes back to the Vampires not getting any face time with their own metaplot. The Antediluvians are supposed to be the terrifying apocalyptic villains of the setting, and one got taken out (with minimal effort) by the Kue-Jin and the Technocracy.</div> </div> </div> </div>???Why do you say Minimal Effort? It was a week of constant fighting against 3 beings just one step below Ravnos himself, that ends with Magical Nuclear Weapons used on him, and then him being blasted with a magically enhanced quadruple sunburst... If this is minimal effort what would you consider maximum effort? Ravnos needed more stuff to take him out then any of the chumps in the Gehenna book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-18T10:50:50-07:00","id":93580,"title":"","content":"Yeah. First off I don't see KotE as a true separate game line from VtM but rather a side line like the VtM historical games.<br /> <br /> Second Ravnos was rampaging for three days before the Technocracy nuked him which doesn't make sense if you think about it, there's no way they couldn't have noticed Ravnos until then. So that could only mean one thing they did know about it before day three.<br /> <br /> And the act of nuking Ravnos is pretty damn overt for the Technocracy, it's not something they'd do without careful consideration. What's more likely is that they sent kill-teams before that but like so many others Ravnos killed them. Leading them to take what is easily a desperate act. Furthermore in <i>Ascension </i>in the Technocracy Civil War it talks about how the WoN terrified them as they never had any idea there were such powerful vampires in existence.<br /> <br /> To me Ravnos's death worked in several ways<i>, </i>especially in regards to the Technocracy blasting him. Remember prior to that the Technocracy considered vampires to be lesser Deviants whom they prefer to largely observe and occasionally meddle with. After the WoN that view has been broken, at least for those higher up in the Union, that view was broken which added to the rising paranoia of the countdown to the ToJ.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-18T11:16:41-07:00","id":93600,"title":"","content":"I really don't mind it as part of the metaplot story. It is a fine way to show things are slowly coming to ahead.<br /> <br /> However, as someone who -started- WoD playing with revised, I really do not like the Week of Nightmares and time after it as the basic setting. Having the apocalypse, red star,etc be still a huge 'maybe' gives room for a lot of stuff that could not be possibly post-week of nightmares.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-18T11:21:27-07:00","id":93607,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/93327-is-it-really-wrong-to-like-the-week-of-nightmares?p=93600#post93600\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I really don't mind it as part of the metaplot story. It is a fine way to show things are slowly coming to ahead.<br /> <br /> However, as someone who -started- WoD playing with revised, I really do not like the Week of Nightmares and time after it as the basic setting. Having the apocalypse, red star,etc be still a huge 'maybe' gives room for a lot of stuff that could not be possibly post-week of nightmares.</div> </div> </div> </div>It still is a maybe even after the week of Nightmares. It just seems like its closer, but well we've had Maelstroms, Antediluvian Fights, and Worldwide Spirit Anomalies before the Week of Nightmares.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-18T21:26:30-07:00","id":94080,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/93327-is-it-really-wrong-to-like-the-week-of-nightmares?p=93553#post93553\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> ???Why do you say Minimal Effort? It was a week of constant fighting against 3 beings just one step below Ravnos himself, that ends with Magical Nuclear Weapons used on him, and then him being blasted with a magically enhanced quadruple sunburst... If this is minimal effort what would you consider maximum effort? Ravnos needed more stuff to take him out then any of the chumps in the Gehenna book.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Technocracy took out an Antediluvian from orbit with zero casualties on their end. Regardless of how big and cool their gun was it doesn't make the situation any less lame. I also don't count the DBZ battle with the Bodhisattvas because it was all so much NPC theater with wailing guitars. We never had any reason to care about these guys until they showed up, and we have no more reason to care about them now that they're gone. The Antediluvians are a presence hovering over and pervading the Vampire setting that establishes its mood and themes. WoN made them into kaiju. Worse still, it made them into yardsticks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-18T22:45:13-07:00","id":94116,"title":"","content":"I cannot stand crossover stuff like the Week of Nightmares or the events that lead to the Sixth Great Maelstrom. It's thoroughly unpleasant. I vastly prefer nWoD's stance on whether or not the other lines exist, and I hate that crossover events drive the plot for each gameline. You could've had a Week of Nightmares without the Technocracy stepping in. You could've had the Sixth Great Maelstrom without a Mummy, Vampire, and Mage involved. Blugh.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-19T02:26:32-07:00","id":94188,"title":"","content":"Nothing wrong with liking it at all. Personally I find it setting-breaking, like I've argued so many times before (just like atamajakki the post above this). But it's really about personal taste. If it works for you and your players, it works.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/deluxe-hunters-hunted-ii\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img692/7017/hh2support.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><a href=\"https://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/deluxe-anarchs-unbound\" target=\"_blank\"> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img703/6636/6kvo.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> <a href=\"https://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/deluxe-mage-the-ascension-20th-anniversary-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img31/2512/25ew.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> <a href=\"https://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/deluxe-w20-book-of-the-wyrm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/507-ignytezero","name":"IgnyteZero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar507_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-19T06:57:12-07:00","id":94239,"title":"","content":"Having a personal preference for something is never wrong.<br /> <br /> That said, I do not share your sentiment. The week of nightmares was horrible, for reasons pretty much as stated by atamajakki and Ama Mizuki above.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/300-hod","name":"HOD","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar300_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"466"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-19T09:19:39-07:00","id":94288,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/93327-is-it-really-wrong-to-like-the-week-of-nightmares?p=93607#post93607\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It still is a maybe even after the week of Nightmares. It just seems like its closer, but well we've had Maelstroms, Antediluvian Fights, and Worldwide Spirit Anomalies before the Week of Nightmares.</div> </div> </div> </div>It isn't maybe anymore, red star is in the sky, all the books basically spell out 'this is the end',etc. It also affects how things change culturally, at least for the garou. Before Week of Nightmares, you could have tribes warring, huge disagreements between septs, but also a lot more hope to push the apocalypse back for few years more. More garou can be born.<br /> <br /> After it, it is a march to the end, the complex tribal wars and disagreements have to be put aside because there is no time. No more garou are born, as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-20T07:04:27-07:00","id":94909,"title":"","content":"I love the Week of Nightmares.<br /> I love the crossover elements.<br /> I love the apocalyptic feel.<br /> I love the fact that it made the Vampires feel IMPORTANT to the wider WoD, in ways that the other game-lines couldn't have understood before then.<br /> I love that it showed that the Garou's ongoing claim that the Final Battle was coming wasn't just empty talk... and that it galvanised them into preparing in full for the coming of the Wyrm.<br /> I love the fact that it demonstrated the Technocracy at their best and most hubristic - the day when the self-appointed guardians of humanity had to back up their claim that they were here for humanity's best interests... and the day when they almost broke the world doing so.<br /> I love the vast, grand scale, because I love the fact that while it may not be every day... it may not even happen for decades at a time... but on some days... Events are grand and vast.<br /> To put it in historical terms... the Cold War is scary because it could have been WWIII. That's what the Week of Nightmares is to me... the moment when things almost broke loose.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>---------------------------------------------<br /> Supporter of Spirits getting full playable splat design come Exalted 3E.<br /> Refugee from the 3rd Great Edition Wars of D&amp;D. <br /> oWoD Latecomer, Exalted Optimist, Scion ST, Trinity Curious","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/955-yue-ryong","name":"Yue Ryong","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar955_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"147"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-20T09:15:11-07:00","id":94987,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yue Ryong</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/93327-is-it-really-wrong-to-like-the-week-of-nightmares?p=94909#post94909\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I love the Week of Nightmares.<br /> I love the crossover elements.<br /> I love the apocalyptic feel.<br /> I love the fact that it made the Vampires feel IMPORTANT to the wider WoD, in ways that the other game-lines couldn't have understood before then.<br /> I love that it showed that the Garou's ongoing claim that the Final Battle was coming wasn't just empty talk... and that it galvanised them into preparing in full for the coming of the Wyrm.<br /> I love the fact that it demonstrated the Technocracy at their best and most hubristic - the day when the self-appointed guardians of humanity had to back up their claim that they were here for humanity's best interests... and the day when they almost broke the world doing so.<br /> I love the vast, grand scale, because I love the fact that while it may not be every day... it may not even happen for decades at a time... but on some days... Events are grand and vast.<br /> To put it in historical terms... the Cold War is scary because it could have been WWIII. That's what the Week of Nightmares is to me... the moment when things almost broke loose.</div> </div> </div> </div>This sums up my sentiments rather well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-20T11:46:43-07:00","id":95102,"title":"","content":"Week of Nightmares had some cool stuff. It had some pretty dumb stuff too. It wasn't much worse than a lot of other metaplots. <br /> <br /> The one I hated was where Baba Yaga, one of the oldest and most badass beings in the entire World of Darkness basically got one shot by a Niktuku while the players were stuck standing there watching. That was just disappointing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-20T12:06:34-07:00","id":95114,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/93327-is-it-really-wrong-to-like-the-week-of-nightmares?p=95102#post95102\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Week of Nightmares had some cool stuff. It had some pretty dumb stuff too. It wasn't much worse than a lot of other metaplots.<br /> <br /> The one I hated was where Baba Yaga, one of the oldest and most badass beings in the entire World of Darkness basically got one shot by a Niktuku while the players were stuck standing there watching. That was just disappointing.</div> </div> </div> </div>That was literally the worst piece of Metaplot in the CWOD for me. Baba Yaga was cool and evocative... her getting ganked in such an awkward lame fashion while the players twiddle their thumbs is... lame sauce.<br /> <br /> It was a bad case of Worfing to use a bit of vernacular I just picked up from the Worfing Thread.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-20T16:07:58-07:00","id":95246,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yue Ryong</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/93327-is-it-really-wrong-to-like-the-week-of-nightmares?p=94909#post94909\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I love the fact that it made the Vampires feel IMPORTANT to the wider WoD, in ways that the other game-lines couldn't have understood before then.</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel it did the opposite. I feel it made sure everyone knew that no matter how big the Vampire was it could still be squashed like a bug by the cooler games and their more important plot. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/93327-is-it-really-wrong-to-like-the-week-of-nightmares?p=95114#post95114\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That was literally the worst piece of Metaplot in the CWOD for me. Baba Yaga was cool and evocative... her getting ganked in such an awkward lame fashion while the players twiddle their thumbs is... lame sauce.<br /> <br /> It was a bad case of Worfing to use a bit of vernacular I just picked up from the Worfing Thread.</div> </div> </div> </div>In essence a reiteration of my feelings vis-a-vis the Ravnos Antediluvian. To be less negative though, despite my strongly held feelings on the subject you aren't wrong to enjoy Week of Nightmares. Like what you like. There's room in this World of Darkness for the both of us.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-21T02:06:57-07:00","id":95472,"title":"","content":"oWoD isn't my specialty, especially since I'm coming in on the 20th Anniverseries where it seems like the Metaplot is being....squashed maybe? Whatever.<br /> <br /> I do have feelings on the Week of Nightmares though, as I keep hearing about it. I may not know all about it, but it more or less comes down to this:<br /> <br /> The story of it feels very cool. The comparison of Ravnos to a kaiju is oddly appropriate, and I'm filled with a sense of awe of just how much went into taking him out, an alignment of accords. Part of me wonders why it didn't start World War Three and the end of the world, as it seems like a great time to knock all the old competitors off their feet, but I digress(besides, I think everyone was just going &quot;Look, we can kill each other later, JUST KILL THAT THING FIRST&quot;). It's modern mythos in a strange and unusual world that promises the end days, and it feels like it. I'm intrigued by the idea of running a game set in that time frame. It's a very cool thing to look at.<br /> <br /> The problems comes from it's utility. I don't feel like I have a use for it outside of running games explicitly in the week. It's not something I want to mandate or have to work around in my normal games.<br /> <br /> So, yeah.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-21T08:05:50-07:00","id":95638,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/93327-is-it-really-wrong-to-like-the-week-of-nightmares#post93327\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I enjoyed the Week of Nightmares.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair enough. Personally, I don't dislike the metaplot, and it has some cool ideas, but I can't help feeling that it should have been an optional scenario, like The Return of the Scarlet Empress for Exalted, rather than &quot;canon&quot; (I hate that word.)<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1441-ersatz","name":"Ersatz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"116"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-22T22:01:35-07:00","id":96723,"title":"","content":"Personally, I hated the Week of Nightmares, as I am a fan of the Ravnos Clan which gets killed off in the Week of Nightmares, and in my opinion combines with the Gangrel going Independent and the departures of the Stargazers to form a triple-threat Jump the Shark moment for oWoD. This is only my opinion, so take these words with a grain of salt.<br /> <br /> In other words, if you liked it, that's fine. In fact, it's not unusual to like the Week of Nightmares. In fact, I was under the impression that liking the Week of Nightmares and the Revised metaplot was the norm for a &quot;proper&quot; WoD Fan, sort of the opposite of what the OP felt, but then again, I found out that was not really the case either.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1579-camilla","name":"Camilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1579_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-22T22:18:04-07:00","id":96725,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Camilla</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/93327-is-it-really-wrong-to-like-the-week-of-nightmares?p=96723#post96723\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally, I hated the Week of Nightmares, as I am a fan of the Ravnos Clan which gets killed off in the Week of Nightmares, and in my opinion combines with the Gangrel going Independent and the departures of the Stargazers to form a triple-threat Jump the Shark moment for oWoD. This is only my opinion, so take these words with a grain of salt.<br /> <br /> In other words, if you liked it, that's fine. In fact, it's not unusual to like the Week of Nightmares. In fact, I was under the impression that liking the Week of Nightmares and the Revised metaplot was the norm for a &quot;proper&quot; WoD Fan, sort of the opposite of what the OP felt, but then again, I found out that was not really the case either.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> What I never really got why that upset people because they made it perfectly clear that it wasn't a 100% thing. Some Ravnos survived, nothing stopping you from playing besides your ST, hell no real issue with doing the same even with a Cappadocian as one could conceivably have survived. Particularly with the Gangrel as a bunch stayed in the Camarilla... And Stargazers are favorites of mine, and they were already rare before, so nothing really changed. It also incentivized detailing the Beast Courts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-23T15:16:09-07:00","id":97072,"title":"","content":"I'm &quot;meh&quot; about the Week of Nightmares. What I absolutely loved, however, was the ToJ News Ticker, which some lovely person archived here:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://rpg-memento.blogspot.co.uk/\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://rpg-memento.blogspot.co.uk/\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://rpg-memento.blogspot.co.uk/\" target=\"_blank\"> http://rpg-memento.blogspot.co.uk/ </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/698-chalicier","name":"chalicier","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"146"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-23T22:50:47-07:00","id":97312,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yue Ryong</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/93327-is-it-really-wrong-to-like-the-week-of-nightmares?p=94909#post94909\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I love the Week of Nightmares.<br /> I love the crossover elements.<br /> I love the apocalyptic feel.<br /> I love the fact that it made the Vampires feel IMPORTANT to the wider WoD, in ways that the other game-lines couldn't have understood before then.<br /> I love that it showed that the Garou's ongoing claim that the Final Battle was coming wasn't just empty talk... and that it galvanised them into preparing in full for the coming of the Wyrm.<br /> I love the fact that it demonstrated the Technocracy at their best and most hubristic - the day when the self-appointed guardians of humanity had to back up their claim that they were here for humanity's best interests... and the day when they almost broke the world doing so.<br /> I love the vast, grand scale, because I love the fact that while it may not be every day... it may not even happen for decades at a time... but on some days... Events are grand and vast.<br /> To put it in historical terms... the Cold War is scary because it could have been WWIII. That's what the Week of Nightmares is to me... the moment when things almost broke loose.</div> </div> </div> </div>+1 To all of this.<br /> <br /> I love the week of nightmares and almost all of the Revised metaplot. The only part I don't use is the Red Star. I always run it as exactly what Yue Ryong said, the apocalypse that ALMOST happened. The only other change from Revised metaplot I usually make is to say that the 6th Great Maelstrom did eventually die down like all the other Maelstroms and that the Shroud did not harden into the Stormwall everywhere, but there are places where it did (thus neatly allowing both Wraith and Orpheus to coexist).<br /> <br /> And anyone who decries crossover clearly has a very advanced ability with selective reading. Crossover elements have been part of nearly every sphere since the very beginning of the World of Darkness.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"<a href=http://imageshack.com/a/img703/6636/6kvo.png target=_blank>http://imageshack.com/a/img703/6636/6kvo.png</a>\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"<a href=http://imageshack.com/a/img692/7017/hh2support.png target=_blank>http://imageshack.com/a/img692/7017/hh2support.png</a>\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2323-killersquirrel59","name":"killersquirrel59","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"558"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-24T13:17:57-07:00","id":97697,"title":"","content":"I remember the news ticker that was rolling that had little items that went from spooky to really scary...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-29T03:58:47-07:00","id":101176,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/93327-is-it-really-wrong-to-like-the-week-of-nightmares?p=96725#post96725\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> What I never really got why that upset people because they made it perfectly clear that it wasn't a 100% thing. Some Ravnos survived, nothing stopping you from playing besides your ST, hell no [...]</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It upsets people because it doesn't only kill off 90% of the clan, it breaks whatever is left. The Jati's and all Ravnos backstory becomes more or less irrelevant. They go from a cool clan with an attitude to stray dogs without a purpose. That's why we hate that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/deluxe-hunters-hunted-ii\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img692/7017/hh2support.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><a href=\"https://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/deluxe-anarchs-unbound\" target=\"_blank\"> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img703/6636/6kvo.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> <a href=\"https://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/deluxe-mage-the-ascension-20th-anniversary-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img31/2512/25ew.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> <a href=\"https://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/deluxe-w20-book-of-the-wyrm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/507-ignytezero","name":"IgnyteZero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar507_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-29T04:06:22-07:00","id":101178,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IgnyteZero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/93327-is-it-really-wrong-to-like-the-week-of-nightmares?p=101176#post101176\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> It upsets people because it doesn't only kill off 90% of the clan, it breaks whatever is left. The Jati's and all Ravnos backstory becomes more or less irrelevant. They go from a cool clan with an attitude to stray dogs without a purpose. That's why we hate that.</div> </div> </div> </div>How? Salubri went through the same thing, the only problem is it happened retroactively as the setting starts without them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-29T04:35:45-07:00","id":101189,"title":"","content":"I'm kinda torn about the Week of Nightmares- from a reader's point of view, I think it's cool. It advances the plot, shows how the different supernatural factions of CWoD mix together when they fight some ancient terror, and it mess things up so much that everyone just feel &quot;the End is Here!&quot;<br /> <br /> From the player/ST's point of view, however, I don't really like it. First, an Antediluvian, one of the ancient blood gods from before the Flood, a being which should be used in order to create horror and be kept as a ST's tool- is getting killed. I hate it when Gods are getting killed, especially while the other Antediluvians still have &quot;loose ends&quot; about their death. It feels like &quot;oh, you wanted to use him? well you can't we killed him. enjoy&quot;. Also, if you already kill a Plot Device, let it die at its own home. Instead, he got killed by a great crossover event- in which the vampires did nothing but eating each other. I mean, if you are doing some giant crossover event, at lest give the vamps the lead role- for it is their boss fight! Finally, I think that the WoN has too much effect on the players. Sure, you can still play one of the surviving Ravanos, but playing a clan which has lost their Antediluvian is a story which is already been told by two different groups in Vampire (and even there we have some unfinished details about the death of their Antediluvians). It is like &quot;hi, I've heard you lost your Antediluvian- join the club! we have cookies!&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-29T13:37:24-08:00","id":354064,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/93327-is-it-really-wrong-to-like-the-week-of-nightmares#post93327\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Though wait I do have one question some have said it was the relics of Fatman and Littleboy that were used on Enoch's Ghost, but that seems very odd since the Smiling Lord harvested his Relic nukes from the desert testing site in America, so they should have been the test nukes like the I have become Shiva nuke. Because if anything wouldn't the Fatman and Little Boy Nukes more likely be in the Hands of Yu Huang or the Japanese Rebels?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not really. The pilot who delivered one of the bombs later stated, that it was not different from other bombing runs. So, I would guess that a relic is formed where it has most spiritual significance. For the nukes their birthplace is Los Alamos and if they become relics they probably form there, not in the air above their respective target towns (nukes were detonated in falling for maximum area coverage).<br /> <br /> I mean, a knife of Jack the Ripper would also not become a relic at the place where it was destroyed, a recycling plant somewhere, but the relic would form in the house Jack lived, in in the very same drawer the knife spend all the time waiting for the next usage.<br /> <br /> <br /> But, the reason why google brought me here:<br /> I run a Werewolf LARP and would like to know, what elements would you use to build up to the Week of Nightmares. What effect would it have on Garou, Changelings, Mages, Sorcerers, Mummies and so on, even before it happens.<br /> <br /> My plan is kind of a game event somewhere in Germany, while the Battle happens in Bangladesh. Setting is that it is the day of the Great Hunt (longest day of the year) and while a lot of mystics predict that the Nightmare Trods will and foretold locations all over the world to await the forces of the fomorians there, there simply aren't enough defender-like changelings there to ward reality. So Helios uses his special day to send Garou to locations not protected by Fae and have the defenders of Gaia ward off their world, too.<br /> <br /> Since it is kind of an anniversary game, I would like to have some foreshadowing, with visions but also ordinary news and possibly events that happen in Germany before the fight (like Ravnos starting to wander off, or killing one another or other vamps and so on). So, any inspiration there ?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-29T18:26:14-08:00","id":354223,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caitiff Primogen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/93327-is-it-really-wrong-to-like-the-week-of-nightmares?p=94080#post94080\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Technocracy took out an Antediluvian from orbit with zero casualties on their end. Regardless of how big and cool their gun was it doesn't make the situation any less lame. I also don't count the DBZ battle with the Bodhisattvas because it was all so much NPC theater with wailing guitars. We never had any reason to care about these guys until they showed up, and we have no more reason to care about them now that they're gone. The Antediluvians are a presence hovering over and pervading the Vampire setting that establishes its mood and themes. WoN made them into kaiju. Worse still, it made them into yardsticks.</div> </div> </div> </div>Completely agree, one hundred percent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2078-alucard","name":"Alucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2078_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"811"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-29T19:18:48-08:00","id":354290,"title":"","content":"I liked the Week of Nightmares, good and bad, and I loved the metaplot. It's one o the biggest reasons I've always been turned off by the nWoD, really. Even with the later psuedometaplot, it was kind of too little, too late.<br /> <br /> As for Ravnos, I was a little bit irked at first, but then I kind of started to like it more and more. I remember reading a line somewhere that was in character from a Ravnos antrtribu basically calling BS on the Lasombra's and Tzimisce's claims about killing off their Antideluvian, and I think that that sort of mentality could make for an amazing story arch if allowed to sort of blossom. Another Sabbat Civil War just before the Final Nights, or maybe to kick them off.<br /> <br /> Anyway, I think it was really cool, actually added something unique and intriguing to the Clan, there just wasn't enough time (real world) to really play with it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://t0.gstatic.com/images?q=tbn:ANd9GcTAO8runv-CR5dodCXgw_8wdJype5yunYCODWdZiBAwUP5WFVv8\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://ksr-ugc.imgix.net/assets/003/593/392/92a29c2836b988505781770a32720148_original.png?v=1428699067&amp;w=700&amp;h=&amp;fit=max&amp;auto=format&amp;lossless=true&amp;s=69ffdde357a0cdd88ee89934622443f9\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img692/7017/hh2support.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img703/6636/6kvo.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1721-beckett","name":"Beckett","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1721_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1077"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-29T19:44:49-08:00","id":354324,"title":"","content":"That Ravnos is one of the sample templates, the Sabbat Heretic, in the Rev Ed Ravnos Clan Book. And yeah it is an interesting idea, especially since at the very least we know [Tzimisce] was not destroyed and the event can even be played through the Transylvania Chronicles. Which makes for some potential ideas for a group running the TC.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-29T21:05:22-08:00","id":354408,"title":"","content":"The CWoD in general, and the CWoD metaplot was always a guilty pleasure sort of thing so I don't think that it's bad to like it With the exception of absolutely awful stuff like the Gypsy's book. CWoD had a lot of awesome stuff you had to separate from not so awesome stuff in the metaplot. I liked the idea they had with the Week of Nightmares even if it got a bit hammy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-29T22:06:35-08:00","id":354456,"title":"","content":"I have mixed feelings about the week of nightmares. I like the idea of it, but I certainly don\u2019t like the execution. It did feel like one of the Vampire game line\u2019s Big Bads was just offhandedly killed because\u2026.Technocracy. There doesn\u2019t seem to be any reason why, if another Antediluvian rises, the Technocracy can\u2019t just do it again. And that sort of precedent is really bothersome to me. <br /> Aside from that, I\u2019ve never liked the idea that an Antediluvian with animalism as an in clan was supposedly in frenzy for days on end. I remember there being a post from one of the Devs explaining why they had chosen the Ravnos founder, and it was basically: it\u2019s a big event that shows the End is here, without altering the clan balance in the main Sects. That reasoning bothered me as well.<br /> Acknowledging that Changeling wasn\u2019t everyone\u2019s favorite, I still felt that they should\u2019ve played a bigger part (or <i>any</i> part for that matter) considering that Chimesrty was being thrown around a lot. I seem to remember that in one of the fluff parts of the book, it even had a Satyr and the effect that the WoN had on him.<br /> I don\u2019t know. Kind of going back to the first point, I think for the giant crossover event that this was supposed to be, more could have been included, and then just having the Technocracy step in and \u201csolve\u201d the event came off as kind of a cop out (imo).<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-30T00:23:49-08:00","id":354534,"title":"","content":"To be honest the Technocracy didn't just offhandedly kill it. First of all the Spirit Nukes wounded it, but it could have recovered from that, and managed to kill those destined to really kill the Antediluvian, while dying themselves as well, and the orbital mirror unleashed after the nukes only managed to kill it because of exact timing, managed unknown by the Technocracy by an Elder Kuei-Jin with a Hsien companion who was the one who actually held the storm at place shielding the Ante from any such attempts. The lesson here was that it took members of three splats unleashing all they had to kill a single antediluvian and it still was all about minute timing.<br /> <br /> It was a carefully orchestrated play where the four battling ancients, the 3 Kuei-Jin and the Antediluvian, were all destined to die but as soon as the Technocracy, Mages that they are, started to twist reality they muddled that fate and it took careful manipulation of circumstances and conditions of the fight to make sure that the destined ending would come about. Also a mere one antediluvian awaking in a frenzy meant millions of casualties and changed how the world worked permanently, Avatar Storm etc., so it really wasn't just about Techies running to help and wiping the floor with the big bad of another line. It was way more than that though all the surrounding circumstances are often forgotten as people only concentrate on the very final blow and who delivered it.<br /> <br /> As a side note I personally didn't really care for the Week of Nightmares and I absolutely abhorred the changes it brought into the mechanics of certain lines, Avatar Storm I'm looking at you. I thought they also missed a lot of metaplot hooks they had planted over the years, Ravana was said to be researching a way to harvest souls of those who died of nuclear blasts to revitalize Lanka and his own power and now suddenly they blasted several spirit nukes right where he had planned it and nothing. Not a single mention about the matter. And more of such let downs were to follow with the actual Gehenna, and other lines similar books, which ignored almost all the story hooks planted over the years, with Vampire basically ending with God just killing all vampires off.... How anticlimatic was that?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-30T04:44:02-08:00","id":354674,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/93327-is-it-really-wrong-to-like-the-week-of-nightmares?p=354456#post354456\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have mixed feelings about the week of nightmares. I like the idea of it, but I certainly don\u2019t like the execution. It did feel like one of the Vampire game line\u2019s Big Bads was just offhandedly killed because\u2026.Technocracy. There doesn\u2019t seem to be any reason why, if another Antediluvian rises, the Technocracy can\u2019t just do it again. And that sort of precedent is really bothersome to me.<br /> Aside from that, I\u2019ve never liked the idea that an Antediluvian with animalism as an in clan was supposedly in frenzy for days on end. I remember there being a post from one of the Devs explaining why they had chosen the Ravnos founder, and it was basically: it\u2019s a big event that shows the End is here, without altering the clan balance in the main Sects. That reasoning bothered me as well.<br /> Acknowledging that Changeling wasn\u2019t everyone\u2019s favorite, I still felt that they should\u2019ve played a bigger part (or <i>any</i> part for that matter) considering that Chimesrty was being thrown around a lot. I seem to remember that in one of the fluff parts of the book, it even had a Satyr and the effect that the WoN had on him.<br /> I don\u2019t know. Kind of going back to the first point, I think for the giant crossover event that this was supposed to be, more could have been included, and then just having the Technocracy step in and \u201csolve\u201d the event came off as kind of a cop out (imo).</div> </div> </div> </div>It is later said that kind of effort was only possible because how the situation unfolded. If the Gehenna comes, that would be impossible because the Union doesn't have the resources to deal with all the Antediluvians. With Ravnos they were extremely lucky that it was only one and was weakened enough for it to work.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1830-history","name":"History","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"158"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-30T07:28:15-08:00","id":354714,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Possessed</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/93327-is-it-really-wrong-to-like-the-week-of-nightmares?p=354534#post354534\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be honest the Technocracy didn't just offhandedly kill it. First of all the Spirit Nukes wounded it, but it could have recovered from that, and managed to kill those destined to really kill the Antediluvian, while dying themselves as well, and the orbital mirror unleashed after the nukes only managed to kill it because of exact timing, managed unknown by the Technocracy by an Elder Kuei-Jin with a Hsien companion who was the one who actually held the storm at place shielding the Ante from any such attempts. The lesson here was that it took members of three splats unleashing all they had to kill a single antediluvian and it still was all about minute timing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Where did you get this? All I read was, that the spirit nukes did kill the Bodhisattvas as well as the fellow who kept the storm going. Therefore clouds dissipated and the sun light reflecting satellites, that were already in place but ineffective until then, started to send sunlight all the way to earth.<br /> <br /> There was not timing issue mentioned anywhere I could find.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-30T07:37:33-08:00","id":354719,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/93327-is-it-really-wrong-to-like-the-week-of-nightmares?p=354714#post354714\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Where did you get this? All I read was, that the spirit nukes did kill the Bodhisattvas as well as the fellow who kept the storm going. Therefore clouds dissipated and the sun light reflecting satellites, that were already in place but ineffective until then, started to send sunlight all the way to earth.<br /> <br /> There was not timing issue mentioned anywhere I could find.</div> </div> </div> </div>Time of Thin Blood specifically page 122 is about the timing. The fellow who kept up the storm survived by the way he was instructed to release the storm at a precise moment.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-30T09:11:13-08:00","id":354785,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/93327-is-it-really-wrong-to-like-the-week-of-nightmares?p=354456#post354456\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have mixed feelings about the week of nightmares. I like the idea of it, but I certainly don\u2019t like the execution. It did feel like one of the Vampire game line\u2019s Big Bads was just offhandedly killed because\u2026.Technocracy. There doesn\u2019t seem to be any reason why, if another Antediluvian rises, the Technocracy can\u2019t just do it again. And that sort of precedent is really bothersome to me.<br /> Aside from that, I\u2019ve never liked the idea that an Antediluvian with animalism as an in clan was supposedly in frenzy for days on end. I remember there being a post from one of the Devs explaining why they had chosen the Ravnos founder, and it was basically: it\u2019s a big event that shows the End is here, without altering the clan balance in the main Sects. That reasoning bothered me as well.<br /> Acknowledging that Changeling wasn\u2019t everyone\u2019s favorite, I still felt that they should\u2019ve played a bigger part (or <i>any</i> part for that matter) considering that Chimesrty was being thrown around a lot. I seem to remember that in one of the fluff parts of the book, it even had a Satyr and the effect that the WoN had on him.<br /> I don\u2019t know. Kind of going back to the first point, I think for the giant crossover event that this was supposed to be, more could have been included, and then just having the Technocracy step in and \u201csolve\u201d the event came off as kind of a cop out (imo).</div> </div> </div> </div>Well to begin with, we know little in the way of concrete information about [Ravnos], including just how long he was in Torpor and any idea what his plans are. We know that when they come out of Torpor they are hungry and that most Ante, most <i>true</i> Ante, have been around for so long they can only sustain themselves on the blood of other vampires. So he's been in Torpor for God knows how long which means that he's going to be starving, meaning he'll be in a hunger frenzy upon waking. That it lasted that long is strange but my two theories about that is 1) the frenzy was not a natural, caused either by his Ante nature or something it was attempting that didn't go as planned, possibly causing its awakening, or 2) he was only initially in frenzy but after feeding on its Childer regained its senses and spent most of the WoN aware of its actions. With the latter I imagine some are asking why some [Ravnos] would being going on a rampage like that if it wasn't in frenzy and all I have to say is why wouldn't it? As far as [Ravnos] knows only a handful of beings could rival or threaten its power on Earth, its fellow Antes, Caine and perhaps the eldest of Kuei-Jin. It's unlikely that [Ravnos] had any real idea of the Technocracy much less its power. Hell few would as Operation Ragnorak was literally an absolute last resort action for them, where they don't care about cost or the damage, they need it dead. And even then they didn't actually kill it, rather they disrupted the cloud cover protecting [Ravnos] from the sun which actually killed it.<br /> <br /> Secondly [Ravnos] had been on a rampage for several days which included magic-created clouds, the consumption of many of its Childer and a lengthy battle between it and the three oldest Kuei-Jin. I'm sorry but that's not something the Technocracy can ignore. If they did nothing then we'd have the opposite reaction with people like me questioning how the Union was asleep at the switch when an undead Blood God was going on a week long rampage.<br /> <br /> And that's the thing, a group like the Technocracy, that spans the globe and tries to control and protect it, can't stay out of these events otherwise it will make them look like some combination of weak, stupid and incompetent for missing out on all that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-30T09:27:07-08:00","id":354815,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Possessed</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/93327-is-it-really-wrong-to-like-the-week-of-nightmares?p=354719#post354719\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Time of Thin Blood specifically page 122 is about the timing. The fellow who kept up the storm survived by the way he was instructed to release the storm at a precise moment.</div> </div> </div> </div>I reread p122 and it doesn\u2019t say anything about specific timing. Perhaps you are wrong on the page number? (admittedly I don\u2019t want to reread the entire book just to look for a timing reference)<br /> I had always been under the impression that the clouds being in place had been there to protect the Bodhisattvas while they fought, since they thought they could win. and after they had died, the clouds were released because Ravnos was then coming after the &quot;snake-man&quot; holding them in place.<br /> And the intensified light of 4 suns would be enough to kill most of the Antediluvians by itself. It\u2019s debatable whether or not that would've done the trick without the spirit nukes beforehand, but we'll never know. So from my point of view, yea the Technocracy can kill off several Antediluvians (those without fortitude certainly) just using the satellites they have in place. And doing so would cost them very little. This obviously assumes they can catch said Antediluvians out in the open, which is a big if admittedly.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Possessed</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/93327-is-it-really-wrong-to-like-the-week-of-nightmares?p=354534#post354534\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> ...managed unknown by the Technocracy by an Elder Kuei-Jin with a Hsien companion who was the one who actually held the storm at place shielding the Ante from any such attempts...</div> </div> </div> </div> for this part, I\u2019m curious why you decided the 4<sup>th</sup> being was Hsien? I had never been under that impression before.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>History</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/93327-is-it-really-wrong-to-like-the-week-of-nightmares?p=354674#post354674\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is later said that kind of effort was only possible because how the situation unfolded. If the Gehenna comes, that would be impossible because the Union doesn't have the resources to deal with all the Antediluvians. With Ravnos they were extremely lucky that it was only one and was weakened enough for it to work.</div> </div> </div> </div> Personally I don\u2019t necessarily think they have the resources to deal with <i>all</i> of the Antediluvians. I do think they have the resources to deal with several of them at least. And in my mind, even that is an issue. Vampires (Kindred/Cainites) weren\u2019t able to do anything about it but deal with the side consequences of it merely being awake. The only way the Vampire line was really involved is if you consider KotE to be in the realm of Vampire, which some people do. Even that is still kind of off-putting to me since nothing from VtM was able to help with their own Big Bads.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-30T13:53:35-08:00","id":355077,"title":"","content":"The way I see it, the Technocracy failed, it was only then that they realized their own paradigm was not stronger than the Cainites as they had always believed. From what I recall it was Ravnos that actually created the storm (at least in part), and both an entire sept of Lupines and 3 bodhisattvas fought him. He essentially changed reality, both summoning his childer and literally bringing dreams and nightmares to life to fight. It was only after he slew them (and all of the Mages in there too), all that the Technocracy was able to do is finally pierce it at all, and even then, as was mentioned above, it was both their literal last resort and even then, only barely worked against a severely weakened creature they had no idea even existed.<br /> <br /> Ravnos is typically considered one of the weakest (in the physical sense) of the Antediluvians, though who could say for sure. I think it was meant to be a two pronged attack, as both Mage's and Kindred of the East are written to encourage a sort of sense of superiority, and (especially for Mages), the actual reality of reality just pimp slapped them in the face. They would not be able to do that again, and even if they could, it's incredibly unlikely that any other Antediluvian would be caught with so many things favoring the Technocracy, (he was still half asleep, had not fed, not at full power, and they had so many other powerful allies helping them out).<br /> <br /> The worlds largest and strongest group of mages just found out the Magick isn't the strongest thing in existence. The Kuei-Jin just lost some of their strongest and oldest member against 1 barbarian Cainite, and managed to royally F-up the balance of the living and the spirit worlds in the process, to no avail whatsoever.<br /> <br /> What's worse, the Technocracies big gun, FAILED. It didn't kill Ravnos. Their nuke, (&quot;magick&quot;ally enhanced to kill supernaturals) failed. It didn't work. It killed everything else that Ravnos hadn't yet, but not him, their actual target. The only way they even managed to hurt him was because they finally managed to get through the clouds, that is to say, that the people that had been keeping it up had finally died.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://t0.gstatic.com/images?q=tbn:ANd9GcTAO8runv-CR5dodCXgw_8wdJype5yunYCODWdZiBAwUP5WFVv8\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://ksr-ugc.imgix.net/assets/003/593/392/92a29c2836b988505781770a32720148_original.png?v=1428699067&amp;w=700&amp;h=&amp;fit=max&amp;auto=format&amp;lossless=true&amp;s=69ffdde357a0cdd88ee89934622443f9\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img692/7017/hh2support.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img703/6636/6kvo.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1721-beckett","name":"Beckett","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1721_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1077"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-30T13:53:48-08:00","id":355078,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/93327-is-it-really-wrong-to-like-the-week-of-nightmares?p=354815#post354815\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally I don\u2019t necessarily think they have the resources to deal with <i>all</i> of the Antediluvians. I do think they have the resources to deal with several of them at least. And in my mind, even that is an issue. Vampires (Kindred/Cainites) weren\u2019t able to do anything about it but deal with the side consequences of it merely being awake. The only way the Vampire line was really involved is if you consider KotE to be in the realm of Vampire, which some people do. Even that is still kind of off-putting to me since nothing from VtM was able to help with their own Big Bads.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well that's more of a flaw in VtM itself than the WoN. Most of the 4th Generation vampires that could have attempted to fight him were either in Torpor, not in the area, MIA, a Ravnos and therefore subjected to the madness hitting the Clan or perhaps too selfish/afraid to approach [Ravnos] much less fight him. In fact the oldest 4thGen, non-Ravnos vampire I know in India is the Tzimisce Kartarirya who was one of the first Childer of [Tzimisce]* and probably would have fought [Ravnos] but she was in Torpor.<br /> <br /> On the other hand we have the Kuei-Jin Bodhisattva which are much... well I want to say active but that's not really the right word but they don't succumb to feeding restrictions, slipping into incredibly long Torpor and generally avoiding the game of Kindred politics, preferring to live in seclusion and sometimes helping their younger kin with their struggles on the path of enlightenment. And of course in theory any Kuei-Jin can become one.<br /> <br /> Then given the connection, whether real or imagined, between [Ravnos] and the Yama King Ravana and the fact that those who tried to divine what was going on kept on seeing [Ravnos] in the form of Ravana, is it any surprise that those Bodhisattva would go out to try and stop whatever the apparent Yama King is attempting to do?<br /> <br /> And for the record I do consider the KotE line a part of VtM as it was intended to in the beginning. Hell the KotE Rulebook needs a VtM Rulebook to actually play the game, something I both love and hate.<br /> <br /> *There's a bit of disagreement over whether Kartarirya or Ionache were the first Childe of [Tzimisce]. One of the DA books lists Ionache while the Rev Ed CB lists Kartarirya. It's been assumed that Kartarirya is the first Childe but because she spent much of her existence in India, the Kindred of Europe at the time had forgotten about her.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-30T14:05:52-08:00","id":355103,"title":"","content":"KotE is kind of weird. It's probably one of the worst books (rules wise or how it fits into the VtM setting) ever done, and while I accept it as part of VtM, I think it would have been infinitely better for both if it had not been. It sort of fits, but not really.<br /> <br /> Or to put it a different way, KotE is a terrible VtM game, but as a generic game unto itself, it's not bad.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://t0.gstatic.com/images?q=tbn:ANd9GcTAO8runv-CR5dodCXgw_8wdJype5yunYCODWdZiBAwUP5WFVv8\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://ksr-ugc.imgix.net/assets/003/593/392/92a29c2836b988505781770a32720148_original.png?v=1428699067&amp;w=700&amp;h=&amp;fit=max&amp;auto=format&amp;lossless=true&amp;s=69ffdde357a0cdd88ee89934622443f9\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img692/7017/hh2support.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img703/6636/6kvo.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":1721,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1721-beckett","user":"Beckett","date":". 12-30-2014, 05:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1721-beckett","name":"Beckett","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1721_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1077"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-30T18:40:31-08:00","id":355295,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AkatsukiLeader13</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/93327-is-it-really-wrong-to-like-the-week-of-nightmares?p=354785#post354785\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well to begin with, we know little in the way of concrete information about [Ravnos], including just how long he was in Torpor and any idea what his plans are. We know that when they come out of Torpor they are hungry and that most Ante, most <i>true</i> Ante, have been around for so long they can only sustain themselves on the blood of other vampires. So he's been in Torpor for God knows how long which means that he's going to be starving, meaning he'll be in a hunger frenzy upon waking. That it lasted that long is strange but my two theories about that is 1) the frenzy was not a natural, caused either by his Ante nature or something it was attempting that didn't go as planned, possibly causing its awakening, or 2) he was only initially in frenzy but after feeding on its Childer regained its senses and spent most of the WoN aware of its actions. With the latter I imagine some are asking why some [Ravnos] would being going on a rampage like that if it wasn't in frenzy and all I have to say is why wouldn't it? As far as [Ravnos] knows only a handful of beings could rival or threaten its power on Earth, its fellow Antes, Caine and perhaps the eldest of Kuei-Jin. It's unlikely that [Ravnos] had any real idea of the Technocracy much less its power. Hell few would as Operation Ragnorak was literally an absolute last resort action for them, where they don't care about cost or the damage, they need it dead. And even then they didn't actually kill it, rather they disrupted the cloud cover protecting [Ravnos] from the sun which actually killed it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ravnos is a master of Animalism and Conquer the Beast is a meer 6th generation power. It allows him to enter and leave frenzy at will.<br /> <br /> There's no reason for him to go on a crazy murder millions rampage. Even if his blood pool is like 65 or somewhere around there that just means he has to chow down on seven neonates to be full up on blood. Going on a blood crazy rampage against his childer and the entire nation of Bangladesh will only wake up other 4th and 3rd gens, draw the attention of Caine, Bodhisattvas, Mages, Werewolves and anything else out there, some of which he can deal with without much problems, others of which would be dangerous even for him. He hasn't survived 10,000 years by being stupid. He can just sit back and spawn an army of new 4th generation childer and roll over the Cathayans in his own private war like the master of jyhad he supposedly is.<br /> <br /> Also, how can someone with Chimestry 10 (having the power to rewrite reality) and Fortitude 10 be one of the weakest Antes? Sounds like a combination for one of the strongest.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2078,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2078-alucard","user":"Alucard","date":". 12-30-2014, 09:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2078-alucard","name":"Alucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2078_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"811"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-30T18:41:21-08:00","id":355296,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Beckett</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/93327-is-it-really-wrong-to-like-the-week-of-nightmares?p=355077#post355077\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The way I see it, the Technocracy failed, it was only then that they realized their own paradigm was not stronger than the Cainites as they had always believed. From what I recall it was Ravnos that actually created the storm (at least in part), and both an entire sept of Lupines and 3 bodhisattvas fought him. He essentially changed reality, both summoning his childer and literally bringing dreams and nightmares to life to fight. It was only after he slew them (and all of the Mages in there too), all that the Technocracy was able to do is finally pierce it at all, and even then, as was mentioned above, it was both their literal last resort and even then, only barely worked against a severely weakened creature they had no idea even existed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Details on the actual fight are somewhat limited, but there doesn\u2019t seem to be any indication that [Ravnos] used either Animalism or Chimestry (purposefully). The text just indicates that there is a fight and that people have visions of a monster (interpreted as the Demon King Ravana) fighting 3 Bodhisattvas (represented as Crane, Tiger and Dragon, I think). The text said it \u201cbarely worked\u201d but the story part just says the sunlight melted him to ash, kind of matter of factly.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Beckett</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/93327-is-it-really-wrong-to-like-the-week-of-nightmares?p=355077#post355077\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Ravnos is typically considered one of the weakest (in the physical sense) of the Antediluvians, though who could say for sure.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not trying to be argumentative, but I\u2019ve never heard this point of view, and in fact I\u2019d wager that [Ravnos] is physically more powerful than at least a few of the other Antediluvians (Set, Tremere, Giavanni all come to mind). That\u2019s about \u00bc of the known Antediluvians right out.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Beckett</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/93327-is-it-really-wrong-to-like-the-week-of-nightmares?p=355077#post355077\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> The worlds largest and strongest group of mages just found out the Magick isn't the strongest thing in existence.</div> </div> </div> </div>The opposite would seem to be true (at least to me). They found out that there are giant scary monster they didn\u2019t know existed, and they used their resources to obliterate it. Magick did prove to be stronger.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AkatsukiLeader13</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/93327-is-it-really-wrong-to-like-the-week-of-nightmares?p=355078#post355078\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well that's more of a flaw in VtM itself than the WoN. Most of the 4th Generation vampires that could have attempted to fight him were either in Torpor, not in the area, MIA, a Ravnos and therefore subjected to the madness hitting the Clan or perhaps too selfish/afraid to approach [Ravnos] much less fight him. In fact the oldest 4thGen, non-Ravnos vampire I know in India is the Tzimisce Kartarirya who was one of the first Childer of [Tzimisce]* and probably would have fought [Ravnos] but she was in Torpor.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thinking about this has made me come to the realization that this is what I both liked and hated about the WoN. I like the epic feel of it. The story of it works fine. So if this were a novel it would be enjoyable.<br /> For a game though, there is literally nothing PCs (of basically any of the game lines) can do to affect it. There is nothing for PCs to do. And most of the time, it won\u2019t even be something they are aware of. So it just sort of happens, and PCs have to deal with some situational side effects, and then it\u2019s over. I seem to remember the book suggesting you can have the players make up a group that goes in to investigate and gets slaughtered, just so the players are aware of what\u2019s going on. That seems like a waste.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-30T21:13:42-08:00","id":355435,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/93327-is-it-really-wrong-to-like-the-week-of-nightmares?p=355295#post355295\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ravnos is a master of Animalism and Conquer the Beast is a meer 6th generation power. It allows him to enter and leave frenzy at will.<br /> <br /> There's no reason for him to go on a crazy murder millions rampage. Even if his blood pool is like 65 or somewhere around there that just means he has to chow down on seven neonates to be full up on blood. Going on a blood crazy rampage against his childer and the entire nation of Bangladesh will only wake up other 4th and 3rd gens, draw the attention of Caine, Bodhisattvas, Mages, Werewolves and anything else out there, some of which he can deal with without much problems, others of which would be dangerous even for him. He hasn't survived 10,000 years by being stupid. He can just sit back and spawn an army of new 4th generation childer and roll over the Cathayans in his own private war like the master of jyhad he supposedly is.<br /> <br /> Also, how can someone with Chimestry 10 (having the power to rewrite reality) and Fortitude 10 be one of the weakest Antes? Sounds like a combination for one of the strongest.</div> </div> </div> </div>Reading through the most complete account of the Week of Nightmares in <i>Time of Thin Blood</i> it actually states something <i>interesting</i>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Time of Thin Blood, Pg. 125</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">As vampires age, they must feed upon increasingly potent blood. First, the blood of animals no longer sustains them. After several centuries, only the vitae of other vampires can satisfy their thirst. The true Antediluvians are <i>more than 10 millennia old</i>. They passed the &quot;Methuselah's Thirst&quot; stage long ago.</div> </div> </div> </div>So yeah [Ravnos] could not slake his thirst on just any vampire but those of the most potent blood, those of the lowest Generations.<br /> <br /> Also just because they're 4th Gen doesn't make newly Embraced vampires stronger, they have to grow into that strength and power first.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-30T21:50:13-08:00","id":355463,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AkatsukiLeader13</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/93327-is-it-really-wrong-to-like-the-week-of-nightmares?p=355435#post355435\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Reading through the most complete account of the Week of Nightmares in <i>Time of Thin Blood</i> it actually states something <i>interesting</i>.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> So yeah [Ravnos] could not slake his thirst on just any vampire but those of the most potent blood, those of the lowest Generations.<br /> <br /> Also just because they're 4th Gen doesn't make newly Embraced vampires stronger, they have to grow into that strength and power first.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, instead of 6-7 13th generation vampires, he could use two sixth gens instead.<br /> <br /> They can blood buff their physical stats to 10 right of the bat, and given their enormous bloodpool of 50, they would have much more stamina then most opponents, able to use what disciplines they do know over and over again. So, they would be much more formidable than the average neonate.<br /> <br /> What's a few decades or even centuries to a creature like Ravnos? A blink of an eye. Once he's woken up the Cathayans of Southeast Asia should be doomed. Sure it'll be a long war, but it's one they can't win.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2078-alucard","name":"Alucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2078_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"811"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-30T22:19:40-08:00","id":355478,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AkatsukiLeader13</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/93327-is-it-really-wrong-to-like-the-week-of-nightmares?p=355435#post355435\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> So yeah [Ravnos] could not slake his thirst on just any vampire but those of the most potent blood, those of the lowest Generations.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mind you, I\u2019m not about to disagree with a quote directly out of a book, but doesn\u2019t this logic reduce all true Antediluvians to mindless rampaging blood gods? Several of the Antediluvians had been seen in the last 1000 or so years acting coherently (relatively speaking). Is there a magical point between 9 and 10 thousands years of age that they lose control? Or do they specifically have to continuously embrace and eat Childer to stop from like a wight? Just an odd thought.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AkatsukiLeader13</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/93327-is-it-really-wrong-to-like-the-week-of-nightmares?p=355435#post355435\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Also just because they're 4th Gen doesn't make newly Embraced vampires stronger, they have to grow into that strength and power first.</div> </div> </div> </div> I don\u2019t know\u2026a horde of 4<sup>th</sup> generation shovelheads will be more effective than 13<sup>th</sup> generation ones.<br /> And if we go by Baba Yaga\u2019s childe, apparently you can accumulate 30 or so dots of disciplines in about 8 years.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-31T01:21:12-08:00","id":355536,"title":"","content":"About the precise timing, on page 122:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Time of Thin Blood, p.122</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;A little longer,&quot; Tieh Ju whispered to the snake-man. &quot;Just a little longer.&quot; The Way burned in her long-dead heart as the universe moved to restore its balance. The time to stop acting hurried closer, closer. She bit her own cheek and sprayd a mouthful of her blood into the wind.</div> </div> </div> </div>Before this on page 121:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Time of Thin Blood p.121</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Around them, the Iron Chrysanteum's acolytes swatted away the ghosts and demons. More and more, however, she felt her attention drawn to the thick, churning clouds that drenched her and her students. Something more than the battle disturbed those clouds. She extended her subtle senses and felt the aircraft moving above the clouds, pushing at them with magical breath. <i>The Five Metal Dragons. </i><i>Of course they would be here.</i> She calmed her mind and felt the Way whisper in her soul. <i>Too soon</i>, it said. She turned to the serpent-man and asked, &quot;Honored sir, do you believe you could thicken the clouds?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>As for why I consider the snake-man Hsien I'll guide your attention towards p.116. I wont quote the whole chapter but there Chou Li, the serpent-man, is reclined on a silken cushion in a temple and one of his four companions is identified as Shangguan who is described to be a &quot;grinning monkey-man&quot;. Also the Hsien magic could be, especially since Tieh Ju lends her help, powerful enough to hold the storm in place. The Hsien are the only group of being in WoD to have amongst their number both serpent-men and monkey-men, in addition to badger-, carp- and cat-men, so it makes sense. Especially since the serpent man in question began his story at his favorite temple and after all was said and done returned back to rebuild his temple, and the Hsien are the little-gods. But no the story does not directly name him as a Hsien but the only alternative is that he would be Nagah which is not only highly unlikely, he is acting alone not as a part of team of three, but also improbable as the Nagah do not really have the magics to hold storms in place agaisnt a group of Mages trying to part them, they are Gaias judges not her meteorologists.<br /> <br /> How is this misconception coming up again even though I pointed it out earlier?<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Beckett</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">What's worse, the Technocracies big gun, FAILED. It didn't kill Ravnos. Their nuke, (&quot;magick&quot;ally enhanced to kill supernaturals) failed. It didn't work. It killed everything else that Ravnos hadn't yet, but not him, their actual target. The only way they even managed to hurt him was because they finally managed to get through the clouds, that is to say, that the people that had been keeping it up had finally died.</div> </div> </div> </div>The one's keeping the storm in place did not die, they awaited for the right moment to release the storm as per my quote above (the first one). Note how Chou Li is the one who has held the storm in place (see my 2nd quote) and consider this:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Time of Thin Blood p.125</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Chou Li sat three days and nights where Tieh Ju had sunk into the ground.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is after the death of [Ravnos] who died right in front of Chou Li after he had released the storm and the sunlight, magnified by the Technocracy, hit [Ravnos]. Those who held the storm at place were just outside of the spirit nukes range though even they felt the warmth of it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-31T02:28:54-08:00","id":355549,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Possessed</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/93327-is-it-really-wrong-to-like-the-week-of-nightmares?p=355536#post355536\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">About the precise timing, on page 122:<br /> As for why I consider the snake-man Hsien I'll guide your attention towards p.116. I wont quote the whole chapter but there Chou Li, the serpent-man, is reclined on a silken cushion in a temple and one of his four companions is identified as Shangguan who is described to be a &quot;grinning monkey-man&quot;. Also the Hsien magic could be, especially since Tieh Ju lends her help, powerful enough to hold the storm in place. The Hsien are the only group of being in WoD to have amongst their number both serpent-men and monkey-men, in addition to badger-, carp- and cat-men, so it makes sense. Especially since the serpent man in question began his story at his favorite temple and after all was said and done returned back to rebuild his temple, and the Hsien are the little-gods. But no the story does not directly name him as a Hsien but the only alternative is that he would be Nagah which is not only highly unlikely, he is acting alone not as a part of team of three, but also improbable as the Nagah do not really have the magics to hold storms in place agaisnt a group of Mages trying to part them, they are Gaias judges not her meteorologists.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> That is really interesting. I\u2019ve only ever skimmed through the Land of 8 Million Dreams (and that was years and years ago) because none of my group wanted anything to do with Changeling at the time. I had assumed it was a Nagah since I'm more familiar with them. In the beast courts, Nagah do operate solitarily, though I think that has more to do with the fact that there wasn\u2019t a breed book out for them when the hengeyokai book came out, so not all of the information matches. And they have an affinity for water, so storm gifts and rites certainly weren\u2019t out of the question. Hsien does make a bit more sense though.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-31T08:58:37-08:00","id":355785,"title":"","content":"I'm not really well versed in Masquerade but I do like it and Week of Nightmares is an important metaplot event, it's just that this more or less establishes Antediluvians as exactly what I didn't want to be true about Gehenna; Mindless OM NOM NOM NOM NOM<br /> <br /> I don't know it's just that it kind of makes the Antediluvians completely uninteresting and without the Time of Judgement book I would've just assumed they were all going to just kill everything with no forethought.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2111-doeman","name":"DoeMan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"68"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-31T11:42:29-08:00","id":355915,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/93327-is-it-really-wrong-to-like-the-week-of-nightmares?p=355295#post355295\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, how can someone with Chimestry 10 (having the power to rewrite reality) and Fortitude 10 be one of the weakest Antes? Sounds like a combination for one of the strongest.</div> </div> </div> </div>Seriously. For the flat-out ability to withstand physical damage I'd think Ennoia would be the only antediluvian able to equal or exceed Ravnos.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-31T12:46:05-08:00","id":355978,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/93327-is-it-really-wrong-to-like-the-week-of-nightmares?p=355296#post355296\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Details on the actual fight are somewhat limited, but there doesn\u2019t seem to be any indication that [Ravnos] used either Animalism or Chimestry (purposefully). The text just indicates that there is a fight and that people have visions of a monster (interpreted as the Demon King Ravana) fighting 3 Bodhisattvas (represented as Crane, Tiger and Dragon, I think). The text said it \u201cbarely worked\u201d but the story part just says the sunlight melted him to ash, kind of matter of factly.<br /> <br /> Not trying to be argumentative, but I\u2019ve never heard this point of view, and in fact I\u2019d wager that [Ravnos] is physically more powerful than at least a few of the other Antediluvians (Set, Tremere, Giavanni all come to mind). That\u2019s about \u00bc of the known Antediluvians right out.<br /> <br /> The opposite would seem to be true (at least to me). They found out that there are giant scary monster they didn\u2019t know existed, and they used their resources to obliterate it. Magick did prove to be stronger.</div> </div> </div> </div>What I mean is, their plans, while in the end where successful, failed in the way they believed it would. Their &quot;big gun&quot; didn't obliterate the target, which might have been a major paradigm shifting moment of it's own, realizing just how little you and your fellows understood. Also, I agree, not trying to be argumentative, just saying from my POV. A lot of things are left a bit vague, and there are other little bits thrown in from different books.<br /> <br /> As for the Ravnos being the weaker of the Antediluvians, I mean in the sense that he (she) was known more for being a trickster than a warrior. Not that the Mages would have known this, and also being one of the weaker Antediluvians isn't saying that much. It's arguable if either Tremere or Giovanni, especially at this moment are even Antediluvians, but it was a suggestion I've heard somewhere, (it might have been online back in the old WW forums one of the devs talking about how Ravnos was really and truly dead?) or in another book. Or it could be wrong.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://t0.gstatic.com/images?q=tbn:ANd9GcTAO8runv-CR5dodCXgw_8wdJype5yunYCODWdZiBAwUP5WFVv8\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://ksr-ugc.imgix.net/assets/003/593/392/92a29c2836b988505781770a32720148_original.png?v=1428699067&amp;w=700&amp;h=&amp;fit=max&amp;auto=format&amp;lossless=true&amp;s=69ffdde357a0cdd88ee89934622443f9\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img692/7017/hh2support.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img703/6636/6kvo.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1721-beckett","name":"Beckett","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1721_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1077"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-31T22:59:01-08:00","id":356294,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/93327-is-it-really-wrong-to-like-the-week-of-nightmares?p=355478#post355478\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don\u2019t know\u2026a horde of 4<sup>th</sup> generation shovelheads will be more effective than 13<sup>th</sup> generation ones.<br /> And if we go by Baba Yaga\u2019s childe, apparently you can accumulate 30 or so dots of disciplines in about 8 years.<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>He was quite a notable exception, but I think it was justified. He was a high level KGB operative in his mortal life. Intelligent, disciplined, used to hard training and willing to engage in life risking battle for his beliefs. Anyone that is embraced who holds all of those attributes will advance much faster than the average vampire, providing they survive said battles.<br /> <br /> If Ravnos were to embrace, say, some Gurkha special operations soldiers, I'd imagine that they too would also accrue power at an accelerated pace, the one limit being what Ravnos wished to teach.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Beckett</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/93327-is-it-really-wrong-to-like-the-week-of-nightmares?p=355978#post355978\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> As for the Ravnos being the weaker of the Antediluvians, I mean in the sense that he (she) was known more for being a trickster than a warrior. Not that the Mages would have known this, and also being one of the weaker Antediluvians isn't saying that much. It's arguable if either Tremere or Giovanni, especially at this moment are even Antediluvians, but it was a suggestion I've heard somewhere, (it might have been online back in the old WW forums one of the devs talking about how Ravnos was really and truly dead?) or in another book. Or it could be wrong.</div> </div> </div> </div>She won a full fledged open war with clan Gangrel.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Eventually, Ennoia and Ravana had a &quot;falling-out&quot;. Something happened to drive them to one another's throats. They fought for decades; they flung their childer at one another, and even encouraged their childer to Embrace new fledglings as soldiers. Ennoia's broods were far stronger, by all accounts, but Ravana was far more cunning and wielded the powers of deception.<br /> At last, Ravana called down some kind of unholy devastation from the sky to destroy or disable most of Ennoia's forces. The handful that survived fled west into Europe or Africa. The survivors then fought amongst themselves, scattering north, south and west. Those who went north latched onto the progenitors of Siberian tribes and the Vikings. Those who went south prowled the African plains above the Sahara to become the shape-changers of the Serengeti. The few vampires who fled eastward were presumed destroyed. The majority went west; it is from these that most of the Gangrel clan traces its lineage. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2078,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2078-alucard","user":"Alucard","date":". 01-01-2015, 02:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2078-alucard","name":"Alucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2078_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"811"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-01T07:07:38-08:00","id":356601,"title":"","content":"Ravana is not Zapathasura, (who himself may or may not be Ravnos), but the forth childer of Zapathasura the broke away and became an infernalist (or from a KotE perspective possibly a Yama King). It's a convoluted tale that's probably more BS than true, as Ennonia (also not the 3rd Gen Gangrel founder, but some sort of 4th Gen child of the Antediluvian that created both the Gangrel and the Ravnos as one line, thus making the two Clans actually two Bloodlines, with the Gangrel failing to fulfill their duty in destroying the KofE/Yama Kings/all supernaturals).<br /> <br /> Both of the Clan Book accounts on the bit of history well, self contradictory and convoluted. Most likely what truly happened is closer to Ravnos wanted India to be his exclusively, and was having a lot of trouble, both with other Cainites edging their way in and also the &quot;indigenous&quot; KotE. Ravnos created this huge philosophy amongst his Clan which was essentially justification to do whatever the hell they wanted, but aimed to focus his brood towards killing all enemies, again with auto justification. Gangrel shows up and Ravnos thinks, hey cool. They are just like me, they will probably help. One thing escalated to another, Ravnos convinces/tricks Gangrel into destroy the 2nd Gen (or helping), thinking that that final act will &quot;free&quot; Gangrel, (ie bringing her over to his POV and solidify their alliance), but Gangrel feels like she had been used and says screw this. 4 out of 5 of Ravnos's other &quot;generals&quot;, (one of them is even believed to be Ennoia/Gangrel as a child of Ravnos!!!), likewise turn against Ravnos, one basically not wanting to fight, another (Ravana) having been tempted to the &quot;demon's side, etc . . . and basically everything goes to hell between the Ravnos and Gangrel &quot;clans&quot;. It's unlikely that Ennoia/Gangrel led an army of anything, as both accounts point out how Gangrel didn't stay with her brood after Embracing them, nor offer instructions for them to Embrace and raise others, nor did she generally stay in one place long enough.<br /> <br /> The Ravnos of India have a historical doctrine of &quot;redeeming&quot; Gangrel, which is to say to turn them to the path of slaying Elders to drink their blood, but not Clan Ravnos, so it's more likely that this skirmish was along the lines of Clan Ravnos hounding Clan Gangrel throughout their travels, and trying to force them into a role of fodder, until this point where the two Clans finally say &quot;that's the last straw&quot;.<br /> <br /> The History on the Gangrel side is primarily from the perspective of an oral history, with multiple cultural contexts added in, and also generally more directed at continuing certain points and events of the story that the specifics of the story itself.<br /> <br /> The History of the Ravnos side is layered into a sort of cult of personality doctrine that contradicts itself a lot, and does not fit with anyone else's tales. It also has been edited to switch around a lot of names, attributing events to the wrong people, as well as switching the context and time frame of various things.<br /> <br /> Now, all that being said, we don't really know what &quot;the truth&quot; is, and the above is mostly what I think may have happened. For example, the Book of Nod suggests that Gangrel was possibly tricked into Frenzying to kill the Second Generation, (and by that I mean given false justification to take part), and thus cursed to be like a beast of the fields, where the Ravnos account says that the gods cursed her for failing her duty, and turning away from further diablerie.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://t0.gstatic.com/images?q=tbn:ANd9GcTAO8runv-CR5dodCXgw_8wdJype5yunYCODWdZiBAwUP5WFVv8\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://ksr-ugc.imgix.net/assets/003/593/392/92a29c2836b988505781770a32720148_original.png?v=1428699067&amp;w=700&amp;h=&amp;fit=max&amp;auto=format&amp;lossless=true&amp;s=69ffdde357a0cdd88ee89934622443f9\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img692/7017/hh2support.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img703/6636/6kvo.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":1721,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1721-beckett","user":"Beckett","date":". 01-01-2015, 10:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1721-beckett","name":"Beckett","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1721_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1077"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-02T04:48:29-08:00","id":357409,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caitiff Primogen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/93327-is-it-really-wrong-to-like-the-week-of-nightmares?p=94080#post94080\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Technocracy took out an Antediluvian from orbit with zero casualties on their end. Regardless of how big and cool their gun was it doesn't make the situation any less lame. I also don't count the DBZ battle with the Bodhisattvas because it was all so much NPC theater with wailing guitars. We never had any reason to care about these guys until they showed up, and we have no more reason to care about them now that they're gone. The Antediluvians are a presence hovering over and pervading the Vampire setting that establishes its mood and themes. WoN made them into kaiju. Worse still, it made them into yardsticks.</div> </div> </div> </div>it wasn't really a zero casualties for the technocrats<br /> the whole region was devasted (and probably the local paradigm shifted as the rakshasas <i>imagined</i> by Ravnos come to life);<br /> they lost a lot of umbral ships that were going around in the Umbra (Maelstroms, Avatar Storms and whatever else);<br /> they sent in an army of kill-teams that were literally butchered by rakshasas, frenzied methuselah and the occasional supernatural bystander;<br /> they bombed him with a friggin' spiritual nuclear bomb and it didn't do a great effect (plus, I don't think these weapons are easy to construct) virtually sterilizing the whole area (not a bad event, for the Thecnocrat point of view, but probably hampering their future actions in the area);<br /> in the end they had to use use a complex orbital system for killing it using the solar light, revealing the extent of their power to the Traditions and probably to all the major associations, supernaturals and &quot;humans&quot;...<br /> <br /> I think that in the end, they killed Ravnos, but the battle was their loss","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>====================================<br /> &quot;Worst English-language User&quot; 2011-2015, 2017 running for the 2018<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/Ed6RV6Z.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></div></div> </div> </div>","edited":{"userid":515,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/515-ryoga84","user":"Ryoga84","date":". 01-02-2015, 09:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/515-ryoga84","name":"Ryoga84","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar515_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-02T09:13:16-08:00","id":357508,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/93327-is-it-really-wrong-to-like-the-week-of-nightmares?p=355478#post355478\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mind you, I\u2019m not about to disagree with a quote directly out of a book, but doesn\u2019t this logic reduce all true Antediluvians to mindless rampaging blood gods? Several of the Antediluvians had been seen in the last 1000 or so years acting coherently (relatively speaking). Is there a magical point between 9 and 10 thousands years of age that they lose control? Or do they specifically have to continuously embrace and eat Childer to stop from like a wight? Just an odd thought.</div> </div> </div> </div>and if, perhaps, [Ravnos] WAS a mindless rampaging blood god?<br /> let's say, what if the [Ravnos] gone on rampage on Bangladesh was not an Antediluvian quietly emerging from Torpor for triggering the Gehenna but an Antediluvian whose Beast had taken control, annihilating his own original master... the most powerful wight the world has ever seen.<br /> <br /> if you can accept this proposition, all the other hints fall in their places.<br /> [Ravnos] was fighting without a comprehensible strategy because it was fighting like a beast,<br /> it couldn't use Animalism to undo its Frenzy because the almost-controlled Frenzy is the wight natural state<br /> it couldn't use Chimestry for rewritting the reality because it would need a conscious endeavor, thus the only Chimestry uses in the whole mess are those instinctive, unconscious and unwilling ones<br /> <br /> and, as a note, it was probably feeding on a lot of methuselah because they, too, were in Torpor, as such their blood reserve was probably limited, it was simply luring them out and feasting on them.<br /> in the end they took it down, like a mad elephant, and the Technocrats sampled it first-hand with a bloodbath....<br /> <br /> <br /> if you take all these consideration in account, Ravnos was in fact the weaker Antediluvian, because with its Beast in charge, it was way much less than an Antediluvian, only the strongest beast that ever ravaged the world.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>====================================<br /> &quot;Worst English-language User&quot; 2011-2015, 2017 running for the 2018<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 